{"what":"Road surface of the existing situation: the ground between the survey's own road lines (DWG layers YOL_SOSE, YOL_TOPRAK, YOL_BORDUR, YOL_KOPRU as cached by the Basemap script). Rings in survey m, to be painted together even-odd (holes included). A fill: where its edge lies on a survey line that line is drawn on top; elsewhere (a straight cut at a street mouth or where a survey line stops) its edge is not a surveyed line and is never drawn as one.","made":"2026-11-13","method":["The survey's road lines, with a straight cut wherever a line stops beside a road (to the line on the other side or to the next line end) and joins over gaps of up to 2 m in the survey's own lines, are made into closed faces. A face is road when the strict surface (next line) covers 60 % of it or more; the whole face is then filled, so its edge is the survey line itself.","Strict surface: the union of the circles that touch a survey road line on two opposite sides (touch directions more than 120 degrees apart; centres on the middle line between the two lines, radius 1 to 13 m), with no building line or wall inside, neither touch point at the end of a line, a middle line of 15 m or more, and either on a street of the town's street file (OpenStreetMap band + 3 m) or between lines up to 9 m apart (tracks, bank roads).","Where the strict surface ends away from any line (a street mouth, the end of a stretch) a straight cut is put between the two survey lines it runs between, and the faces are made again (up to 5 rounds).","Faces covered less than that keep only the strict surface inside them, on its own side of every survey line and cut, with each open edge made one straight edge between its two ends.","A short break in a road (one of its lines stops for up to 20 m) is joined by the band between the two ends that face each other, if no surveyed building and no survey road line lies in it and 75 % or more of its edge is road surface or survey line (6 breaks).","Surveyed buildings are cut out; parts under 40 m2 dropped, and so are parts under 30 m long that touch no other part (15 fragments, 2062 m2): too short to read as a road."],"figures":{"surface_m2":82397,"inside_red_line_m2":30449,"whole_faces_m2":83309,"outline_m":22558,"outline_on_a_survey_road_line_percent":94,"outline_on_a_straight_cut_percent":6,"on_surveyed_buildings_m2":0.0},"limits":"Where the survey draws only one edge of a road, or none (old town streets between house fronts), there is no surface: no edge is invented. Roads wider than 26 m between their lines are not filled.","rings":[[[31239.11,30380.5],[31203.18,30401.74],[31206.16,30406.91],[31241.33,30386.25]],[[30028.1,32041.97],[30036.59,32043.74],[30045.35,32045.94],[30046.83,32046.33],[30050.2,32047.46],[30055.34,32049.12],[30056.97,32049.85],[30058.11,32050.43],[30059.74,32051.53],[30060.62,32052.25],[30065.14,32058.91],[30077.93,32063.37],[30081.06,32061.59],[30083.07,32061.38],[30084.73,32061.98],[30085.3,32062.66],[30088.21,32066.49],[30091.91,32071.46],[30095.7,32069.75],[30088.56,32060.23],[30087.62,32058.79],[30087.87,32057.17],[30088.09,32056.39],[30088.6,32055.96],[30108.29,32046.3],[30113.82,32044.54],[30133.76,32039.86],[30147.21,32036.74],[30151.58,32035.68],[30163.25,32033.22],[30176.92,32031.21],[30220.66,32024.47],[30221.19,32024.61],[30226.56,32024.17],[30226.85,32023.69],[30227.66,32023.38],[30242.66,32021.14],[30251.15,32019.82],[30260.96,32018.11],[30266.24,32016.73],[30269.36,32015.46],[30269.92,32015.46],[30270.53,32015.85],[30274.35,32021.58],[30274.78,32033.0],[30273.65,32035.83],[30278.86,32037.16],[30282.73,32028.48],[30284.84,32023.03],[30281.75,32017.15],[30278.47,32011.74],[30278.96,32010.25],[30287.95,32002.19],[30305.57,31981.62],[30306.51,31980.97],[30315.32,31979.02],[30317.27,31971.09],[30317.63,31968.67],[30319.04,31969.94],[30341.71,31955.92],[30361.27,31945.58],[30366.76,31942.18],[30362.57,31932.71],[30365.19,31930.69],[30370.34,31929.42],[30377.8,31921.9],[30378.11,31920.8],[30389.59,31912.